				<a href="/guides">Guides</a>
				<span>/</span>
				<span>Startpage Search Engine</span>
			</nav>

			<h1>Startpage Search Engine</h1>
			<p class="intro">Google results with complete privacy - no tracking, no profiles, no AI.</p>

			<nav class="toc">
				<h2>Contents</h2>
				<ol>
					<li><a href="#what-is">What is Startpage?</a></li>
					<li><a href="#how-it-works">How Startpage Works</a></li>
					<li><a href="#features">Key Features</a></li>
					<li><a href="#anonymous-view">Anonymous View Explained</a></li>
					<li><a href="#privacy">Privacy & Security</a></li>
					<li><a href="#pros-cons">Pros and Cons</a></li>
					<li><a href="#setup">How to Use Startpage</a></li>
					<li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<section id="what-is">
				<h2>What is Startpage?</h2>
				<p>Startpage is a Dutch search engine that acts as a privacy proxy for Google. When you search on Startpage:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Startpage sends your query to Google anonymously</li>
					<li>Google returns the results to Startpage</li>
					<li>Startpage shows you the results without any tracking</li>
				</ul>
				<p>The result? You get Google's search quality without Google building a profile about you.</p>

				<div class="highlight-box">
					<h3>Quick Facts</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Founded:</strong> 2006 (Netherlands)</li>
						<li><strong>Index:</strong> Google (via proxy)</li>
						<li><strong>AI Features:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Tracking:</strong> None</li>
						<li><strong>Business Model:</strong> Non-tracking ads</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="how-it-works">
				<h2>How Startpage Works</h2>
				<p>Unlike search engines that build their own index, Startpage proxies Google:</p>

				<div class="process-steps">
					<div class="step">
						<span class="step-number">1</span>
						<div>
							<h4>You Search</h4>
							<p>Type your query on startpage.com</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="step">
						<span class="step-number">2</span>
						<div>
							<h4>Startpage Anonymizes</h4>
							<p>Your IP and identifiers are stripped</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="step">
						<span class="step-number">3</span>
						<div>
							<h4>Query Sent to Google</h4>
							<p>Startpage sends the anonymous query</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="step">
						<span class="step-number">4</span>
						<div>
							<h4>Results Returned</h4>
							<p>Google can't identify you from the query</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<p>This means Google never sees your real IP address, browser fingerprint, or any identifying information.</p>
			</section>

			<section id="features">
				<h2>Key Features</h2>

				<div class="feature-grid">
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Anonymous View</h3>
						<p>Browse websites through Startpage's proxy so they can't track you either.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>No Tracking</h3>
						<p>No cookies, no IP logging, no search history stored.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Google Quality</h3>
						<p>Get the same results as Google without the tracking.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>No AI Features</h3>
						<p>Pure search results - no AI summaries or generated content.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>Customizable</h3>
						<p>Themes, languages, regions - all saved locally, not on their servers.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="feature-card">
						<h3>EU-Based</h3>
						<p>Netherlands headquarters means GDPR protection.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="anonymous-view">
				<h2>Anonymous View Explained</h2>
				<p>Anonymous View is Startpage's standout feature. It lets you visit any search result through Startpage's proxy:</p>

				<div class="method-box">
					<h3>How to Use Anonymous View</h3>
					<ol>
						<li>Search on Startpage as normal</li>
						<li>Look for the mask icon or "Anonymous View" link next to results</li>
						<li>Click it to view the page through Startpage's proxy</li>
						<li>The website sees Startpage's IP, not yours</li>
					</ol>
				</div>

				<h3>What Anonymous View Protects</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Your IP address</strong> - Websites see Startpage's IP instead</li>
					<li><strong>Cookies</strong> - Blocked from being set on your browser</li>
					<li><strong>Tracking scripts</strong> - Many are blocked or sandboxed</li>
					<li><strong>Referrer info</strong> - Sites don't know you came from a search</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Limitations</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Some sites don't work well (those requiring login, heavy JavaScript)</li>
					<li>Pages may load slower</li>
					<li>Interactive features may not work</li>
					<li>Not a replacement for a full VPN</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="privacy">
				<h2>Privacy & Security</h2>

				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">Privacy Certified</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<h3>What Startpage Doesn't Collect</h3>
					<ul>
						<li>IP addresses</li>
						<li>Search queries (linked to you)</li>
						<li>Browser fingerprints</li>
						<li>User profiles</li>
						<li>Tracking cookies</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Privacy Certifications</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>EuroPriSe</strong> - European Privacy Seal</li>
						<li><strong>Independent audits</strong> - Regular third-party security reviews</li>
						<li><strong>GDPR compliant</strong> - EU data protection standards</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Ownership Note</h3>
					<p>In 2019, System1 (a US ad company) acquired a majority stake in Startpage. This raised privacy concerns, but Startpage maintains they operate independently and haven't changed their privacy practices. The company remains based in the Netherlands under EU law.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="pros-cons">
				<h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

				<div class="pros-cons">
					<div class="pros">
						<h4>Pros</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Google-quality search results</li>
							<li>No tracking whatsoever</li>
							<li>Anonymous View for browsing</li>
							<li>No AI features</li>
							<li>EU-based (GDPR)</li>
							<li>Clean, simple interface</li>
							<li>No account required</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
					<div class="cons">
						<h4>Cons</h4>
						<ul>
							<li>Can be slower than direct Google</li>
							<li>Sometimes rate-limited by Google</li>
							<li>US company has majority ownership</li>
							<li>Dependent on Google's index</li>
							<li>Anonymous View has limitations</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="setup">
				<h2>How to Use Startpage</h2>

				<div class="browser-section">
					<h3>Set as Default Search Engine</h3>
					<p>Add Startpage as your default search engine using this URL:</p>
					<code class="code-block">https://www.startpage.com/sp/search?query=%s</code>

					<h3>Browser Instructions</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Chrome:</strong> Settings → Search engine → Manage → Add (use URL above)</li>
						<li><strong>Firefox:</strong> Visit startpage.com, click address bar, add search engine</li>
						<li><strong>Safari:</strong> Not available as custom engine (use as homepage instead)</li>
						<li><strong>Edge:</strong> Settings → Privacy → Address bar → Manage → Add</li>
					</ul>

					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine" class="cta-button secondary">Full Setup Guide</a>
				</div>

				<div class="browser-section" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
					<h3>Startpage Browser Extension</h3>
					<p>Startpage offers a browser extension that:</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Sets Startpage as your default search</li>
						<li>Adds privacy protection features</li>
						<li>Available for Chrome, Firefox, and Edge</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="faq">
				<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is Startpage search engine?</h3>
					<p>Startpage is a privacy-focused search engine that proxies Google. You get Google results without Google seeing your IP address, building a profile, or tracking your searches.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Startpage safe to use?</h3>
					<p>Yes. Startpage is based in the Netherlands (EU privacy laws), doesn't store any personal data, and has been certified by EuroPriSe. They've been operating since 2006 with a strong privacy record.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Is Startpage better than DuckDuckGo?</h3>
					<p>It depends on your priorities. Startpage provides Google results (often more comprehensive). DuckDuckGo uses Bing and offers more features like !bangs. Both have excellent privacy. Startpage is EU-based; DuckDuckGo is US-based.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>What is Anonymous View on Startpage?</h3>
					<p>Anonymous View lets you visit search results through Startpage's proxy. The destination website sees Startpage's IP instead of yours, blocking tracking cookies and scripts. It's like a mini-VPN for browsing.</p>
				</div>

				<div class="faq-item">
					<h3>Does Startpage have AI features?</h3>
					<p>No. Startpage shows traditional search results without any AI summaries or generated content. If you want AI-free Google results, Startpage is an excellent choice.</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="next-steps">
				<h2>Next Steps</h2>
				<div class="next-links">
					<a href="/guides/best-private-search-engines">
						<span>Compare</span>
						<strong>Best Private Search Engines</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/set-default-search-engine">
						<span>Setup</span>
						<strong>Set as Default Search</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/duckduckgo-vs-google">
						<span>Compare</span>
						<strong>DuckDuckGo vs Google</strong>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>

